;
; DEVS:NetInterfaces/tap0 -- the same interface, written the way Roadshow's own
; AddNetInterface documents it (Documentation/Reference/AddNetInterface.doc in
; the demo archive).  The keywords are not the same set ours takes, and a stack
; should be measured with a configuration it agrees is well formed:
;
;   * the address is given with ADDRESS/NETMASK and no CONFIGURE line, because
;     CONFIGURE there takes DHCP, AUTO or FASTAUTO and there is no server on
;     this wire;
;   * REQUIRESINITDELAY defaults to YES, which delays the first transmit by
;     about a second on every interface, and nothing here is an Ariadne I;
;   * IPREQUESTS defaults to 32 CMD_READs; eight is plenty for a harness that
;     injects one frame at a time and keeps the device's queue readable.
;
; STATE=ONLINE and not the default.  AddNetInterface.doc: "By default,
; interfaces whose addresses are configured will switch automatically to 'up'
; state ... the alternatives 'online' (implies 'up', but tells the underlying
; network interface driver to go online first)".  Without it the interface is
; configured and the DEVICE is never sent S2_ONLINE, so the first run of this
; harness got `AddNetInterface` returning 0 and a device that had never been
; asked to start.
;
DEVICE=tcpdrill.device
UNIT=0
ADDRESS=10.9.9.1
NETMASK=255.255.255.0
STATE=ONLINE
REQUIRESINITDELAY=NO
IPREQUESTS=8
ARPREQUESTS=4
